{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-0113"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Vegetable and Root-Crop Growing Operations Coordination"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "0113"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :agriculture/vegetable-growing
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:food-security :rural-employment :environmental-stewardship]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :field-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :audit-ledger]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies [:telemetry :optimization :dmn :bpmn]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "VegOpsAdvisor ⊣ Field Operations Governor, langgraph-clj StateGraph
 (langgraph.graph, vegops.operation/build), append-only audit ledger
 (vegops.store/ledger + append-ledger!, MemStore and a DatomicStore
 backed by langchain.db via langchain-store.core). Replaces a
 previously deferred actor: `operation/build` returned a bare Clojure
 closure over the synchronous `run-operation` flow and never touched
 `kotoba-lang/langgraph` at all (its own docstring called it a \"Stub
 for building a langgraph-clj StateGraph\"); `deps.edn` had an empty
 top-level `:deps {}` with langgraph only reachable via `:dev`
 override-deps (nothing to override); no audit ledger existed in the
 repo at all. Now: a genuinely compiled StateGraph
 (`:intake -> :advise -> :govern -> :decide -+-> :commit /
 :request-approval -> :commit / :hold`) with `interrupt-before
 #{:request-approval}` + in-memory checkpointer for real
 human-in-the-loop resume, and BOTH `:commit` and `:hold` durably
 append to the real audit ledger (`store/append-ledger!`) -- a
 back-office OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor for vegetable/root-crop
 field management (tomato/cucumber/cabbage/onion/carrot/potato/
 sweet-potato/watermelon) -- not direct field-equipment operation
 authority and not pesticide-application-decision authority. Four ops
 (`:log-field-record` / `:schedule-field-operation` /
 `:flag-crop-health-concern` / `:order-supplies`), all `:effect
 :propose` only. Five HARD invariants (field-not-registered,
 no-execution, equipment-or-pesticide-decision-blocked, op-not-allowed,
 field-record-invalid) plus independent cost/acreage/confidence
 verification (`vegops.registry`) elaborate this blueprint's Governor.
 Crop-health-concern flagging ALWAYS escalates to a human
 farmer/agronomist via the compiled graph's `:request-approval` node
 (`interrupt-before`, checkpoint-based resume, proven by a new
 `test/vegops/operation_test.cljc` exercising commit / hard-hold /
 escalate-approve / escalate-reject through the REAL compiled graph
 end to end, plus a `clojure -M:dev:run` demo runner producing 4
 distinct real ledger entries). 36 tests / 133 assertions green
 (`clojure -M:dev:test`), clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings, demo
 runnable end-to-end against both Store backends."}
